BEARDEDTEK_INITIAL_HASH='$6$CHANGEME-salt$CHANGEME-hash'
DYOUNG_INITIAL_HASH='$6$CHANGEME-salt$CHANGEME-hash'
ROOT_INITIAL_HASH='$6$CHANGEME-salt$CHANGEME-hash'

# Copy this file to `initial-passwords.env` (no .example suffix,
# gitignored) in this same directory, replacing each value with real
# output of `mkpasswd -m sha-512`.
#
# These are ONE-TIME initial passwords applied only when each account is
# first created (users.mutableUsers = true + initialHashedPassword) — once
# an account exists, whatever the user sets via `passwd` persists across
# every future rebuild, and editing this file has no effect on an
# already-created account. Rotating one after the fact means logging in
# and running `passwd`/`chpasswd` directly, not redeploying.
#
# `source secrets/initial-passwords.env` before any nix command that
# builds/deploys the `young` nixosConfiguration (nixos-anywhere, nixos-
# rebuild switch --target-host, or a local dry-run build) — those all need
# `--impure` too, since these are read via builtins.getEnv rather than a
# file inside the flake (a gitignored file wouldn't be visible to a pure
# flake evaluation anyway).
